  32:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c **** 
  33:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****       (#) Initialize the FMAC low level resources by implementing the HAL_FMAC_MspInit():
  34:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****           (++) Enable the FMAC interface clock using __HAL_RCC_FMAC_CLK_ENABLE().
  35:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****           (++) In case of using interrupts (e.g. access configured as FMAC_BUFFER_ACCESS_IT):
  36:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****                (+++) Configure the FMAC interrupt priority using HAL_NVIC_SetPriority().
  37:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****                (+++) Enable the FMAC IRQ handler using HAL_NVIC_EnableIRQ().
  38:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****                (+++) In FMAC IRQ handler, call HAL_FMAC_IRQHandler().
  39:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****           (++) In case of using DMA to control data transfer (e.g. access configured
  40:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****                as FMAC_BUFFER_ACCESS_DMA):
  41:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****                (+++) Enable the DMA interface clock using __HAL_RCC_DMA1_CLK_ENABLE()
  42:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****                      or __HAL_RCC_DMA2_CLK_ENABLE() depending on the used DMA instance.
  43:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****                (+++) Enable the DMAMUX1 interface clock using __HAL_RCC_DMAMUX1_CLK_ENABLE().
  44:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****                (+++) If the initialization of the internal buffers (coefficients, input,
  45:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****                      output) is done via DMA, configure and enable one DMA channel for
  46:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****                      managing data transfer from memory to memory (preload channel).
  47:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****                (+++) If the input buffer is accessed via DMA, configure and enable one
  48:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****                      DMA channel for managing data transfer from memory to peripheral
  49:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****                      (input channel).
  50:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****                (+++) If the output buffer is accessed via DMA, configure and enable
  51:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****                      one DMA channel for managing data transfer from peripheral to
  52:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****                      memory (output channel).
  53:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****                (+++) Associate the initialized DMA handle(s) to the FMAC DMA handle(s)
  54:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****                      using __HAL_LINKDMA().
  55:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****                (+++) Configure the priority and enable the NVIC for the transfer complete
  56:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****                      interrupt on the enabled DMA channel(s) using HAL_NVIC_SetPriority()
  57:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****                      and HAL_NVIC_EnableIRQ().
  58:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c **** 
  59:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****       (#) Initialize the FMAC HAL using HAL_FMAC_Init(). This function
  60:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****           resorts to HAL_FMAC_MspInit() for low-level initialization.
  61:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c **** 
  62:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****       (#) Configure the FMAC processing (filter) using HAL_FMAC_FilterConfig()
  63:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****           or HAL_FMAC_FilterConfig_DMA().
  64:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****           This function:
  65:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****           (++) Defines the memory area within the FMAC internal memory
  66:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****                (input, coefficients, output) and the associated threshold (input, output).
  67:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****           (++) Configures the filter and its parameters:
  68:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****                (+++) Finite Impulse Response (FIR) filter (also known as convolution).
  69:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****                (+++) Infinite Impulse Response (IIR) filter (direct form 1).
  70:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****           (++) Choose the way to access to the input and output buffers: none, polling,
  71:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****                DMA, IT. "none" means the input and/or output data will be handled by
  72:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****                another IP (ADC, DAC, etc.).
  73:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****           (++) Enable the error interruptions in the input access and/or the output
  74:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****                access is done through IT/DMA. If an error occurs, the interruption
  75:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****                will be triggered in loop. In order to recover, the user will have
  76:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****                to reset the IP with the sequence HAL_FMAC_DeInit / HAL_FMAC_Init.
  77:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****                Optionally, he can also disable the interrupt using __HAL_FMAC_DISABLE_IT;
  78:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****                the error status will be kept, but no more interrupt will be triggered.
  79:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****           (++) Write the provided coefficients into the internal memory using polling
  80:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****                mode ( HAL_FMAC_FilterConfig() ) or DMA ( HAL_FMAC_FilterConfig_DMA() ).
  81:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****                In the DMA case, HAL_FMAC_FilterConfigCallback() is called when
  82:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****                the handling is over.
  83:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c **** 
  84:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****        (#) Optionally, the user can enable the error interruption related to
  85:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****            saturation by calling __HAL_FMAC_ENABLE_IT. This helps in debugging the
  86:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****            filter. If a saturation occurs, the interruption will be triggered in loop.
  87:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****            In order to recover, the user will have to:
  88:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****            (++) Disable the interruption by calling __HAL_FMAC_DISABLE_IT if
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccxFkdJ3.s 			page 3


  89:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****                 the user wishes to continue all the same.
  90:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****            (++) Reset the IP with the sequence HAL_FMAC_DeInit / HAL_FMAC_Init.
