  92:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****        (#) Optionally, preload input (FIR, IIR) and output (IIR) data using
  93:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****            HAL_FMAC_FilterPreload() or HAL_FMAC_FilterPreload_DMA().
  94:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****            In the DMA case, HAL_FMAC_FilterPreloadCallback() is called when
  95:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****            the handling is over.
  96:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****            This step is optional as the filter can be started without preloaded
  97:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****            data.
  98:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c **** 
  99:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****        (#) Start the FMAC processing (filter) using HAL_FMAC_FilterStart().
 100:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****            This function also configures the output buffer that will be filled from
 101:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****            the circular internal output buffer. The function returns immediately
 102:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****            without updating the provided buffer. The IP processing will be active until
 103:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****            HAL_FMAC_FilterStop() is called.
 104:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c **** 
 105:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****        (#) If the input internal buffer is accessed via DMA, HAL_FMAC_HalfGetDataCallback()
 106:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****            will be called to indicate that half of the input buffer has been handled.
 107:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c **** 
 108:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****        (#) If the input internal buffer is accessed via DMA or interrupt, HAL_FMAC_GetDataCallback(
 109:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****            will be called to require new input data. It will be provided through
 110:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****            HAL_FMAC_AppendFilterData() if the DMA isn't in circular mode.
 111:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c **** 
 112:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****        (#) If the output internal buffer is accessed via DMA, HAL_FMAC_HalfOutputDataReadyCallback(
 113:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****            will be called to indicate that half of the output buffer has been handled.
 114:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c **** 
 115:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****        (#) If the output internal buffer is accessed via DMA or interrupt,
 116:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****            HAL_FMAC_OutputDataReadyCallback() will be called to require a new output
 117:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****            buffer. It will be provided through HAL_FMAC_ConfigFilterOutputBuffer()
 118:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****            if the DMA isn't in circular mode.
 119:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c **** 
 120:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****        (#) In all modes except none, provide new input data to be processed via HAL_FMAC_AppendFilt
 121:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****            This function should only be called once the previous input data has been handled
 122:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****            (the preloaded input data isn't concerned).
 123:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c **** 
 124:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****        (#) In all modes except none, provide a new output buffer to be filled via
 125:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****            HAL_FMAC_ConfigFilterOutputBuffer(). This function should only be called once the previo
 126:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****            user's output buffer has been filled.
 127:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c **** 
 128:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****        (#) In polling mode, handle the input and output data using HAL_FMAC_PollFilterData().
 129:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****            This function:
 130:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****            (++) Write the user's input data (provided via HAL_FMAC_AppendFilterData())
 131:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****                 into the FMAC input memory area.
 132:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****            (++) Read the FMAC output memory area and write it into the user's output buffer.
 133:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****            It will return either when:
 134:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****            (++) the user's output buffer is filled.
 135:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****            (++) the user's input buffer has been handled.
 136:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****            The unused data (unread input data or free output data) will not be saved.
 137:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****            The user will have to use the updated input and output sizes to keep track
 138:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****            of them.
 139:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c **** 
 140:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c ****        (#) Stop the FMAC processing (filter) using HAL_FMAC_FilterStop().
 141:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_fmac.c **** 
